{
  "title": "AZ · SAA-C03 개념 위키",
  "description": "한 리전 안에서 서버를 나누어 배치할 장애 분리 단위입니다.",
  "main": "<nav aria-label=\"현재 위치\" class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/concepts/\">개념 위키</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span>AZ <span class=\"full-name\">(Availability Zone)</span></span></nav><div class=\"wiki-layout\"><aside class=\"wiki-toc\"><details open=\"\"><summary>이 문서의 목차</summary><nav aria-label=\"문서 목차\"><ol><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#overview\">개요</a></li><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#guide-1\">여러 AZ에 서비스를 배치하는 방법</a></li><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#guide-2\">리소스의 배치 범위</a></li><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#visual\">구성 한눈에 보기</a></li><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#scenario\">적용 예시</a></li><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#notes\">각주</a></li><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#references\">AWS 공식 문서</a></li><li><a href=\"/concepts/terms/az/#practice\">연관 문제 5개</a></li></ol></nav></details><a class=\"back-index\" href=\"/concepts/\">← 전체 개념 보기</a></aside><div class=\"wiki-main\"><article class=\"term-article\"><header class=\"article-header\"><div class=\"term-meta\"><span>기초</span><span>06 / 62</span></div><h1>AZ <span class=\"full-name\">(Availability Zone)</span></h1></header><section class=\"overview\" id=\"overview\"><h2>개요</h2><p>가용 영역(AZ)은 <strong>한 리전 안에서 장애 영향을 분리하도록 구성한 데이터 센터 집합</strong>입니다. 서로 다른 AZ에 서비스를 나누면 한쪽에 장애가 발생해도 다른 쪽에서 서비스를 계속 제공할 수 있습니다.</p><p>AZ는 서버의 수보다 서버가 놓인 위치를 이해할 때 중요한 개념입니다. 같은 AZ에 서버를 여러 대 두는 것과 여러 AZ에 나누는 것은 대비할 수 있는 장애의 범위가 다릅니다.</p></section><section class=\"wiki-section concept-guide\" id=\"guide-1\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"concept-anchor\" id=\"availability-zone-name\"></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"concept-anchor\" id=\"availability-zone-id\"></span><h2>여러 AZ에 서비스를 배치하는 방법</h2><p>각 AZ에 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/subnet/\">서브넷</a>을 만들고 애플리케이션 서버를 나눠 배치합니다. <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/elb/\">로드 밸런서</a>는 정상 서버에 요청을 전달하고, <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/asg/\">Auto Scaling</a>은 필요한 서버 수를 유지합니다.</p><p>데이터베이스도 장애 전환을 지원하는 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/multiaz/\">Multi-AZ</a> 구성을 검토합니다. 서버만 분산해도 데이터베이스가 한곳에만 있으면 전체 서비스가 그 데이터베이스에 의존합니다.</p></section><section class=\"wiki-section concept-guide\" id=\"guide-2\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"concept-anchor\" id=\"zonal-resources\"></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"concept-anchor\" id=\"regional-resources\"></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"concept-anchor\" id=\"multi-az-design\"></span><h2>리소스의 배치 범위</h2><p>서브넷과 EBS 볼륨은 특정 AZ에 속합니다. EC2에 EBS 볼륨을 연결할 때도 같은 AZ에 있어야 합니다. VPC는 한 리전 안에서 여러 AZ의 서브넷을 포함합니다.</p><p>다른 AWS 계정과 동일한 물리적 AZ를 확인할 때는 계정별로 달라질 수 있는 이름 대신 AZ ID<sup><a aria-label=\"각주 1\" class=\"concept-note-ref\" href=\"#note-1\" id=\"note-ref-1\" role=\"doc-noteref\">[1]</a></sup>를 비교합니다. AZ 간 통신 비용과 지연도 설계에 반영합니다.</p></section><section class=\"visual\" id=\"visual\"><figure class=\"diagram concept-diagram\"><figcaption><b>AZ 장애에 대비하는 구성</b></figcaption><div class=\"diagram-body\"><ol class=\"concept-flow\"><li><strong>정상 서비스</strong><span>여러 AZ에 서버 운영</span></li><li><strong>한 AZ 장애</strong><span>해당 서버로의 요청 중단</span></li><li><strong>다른 AZ 처리</strong><span>남은 서버가 요청 수용</span></li></ol><p class=\"diagram-note\">다른 AZ에 남은 용량이 실제 요청을 처리할 수 있어야 합니다.</p></div></figure></section><section class=\"scenario\" id=\"scenario\"><h2>적용 예시</h2><p>웹 서버를 두 AZ에 배치하고 로드 밸런서로 묶습니다. 한 AZ가 중단되면 정상 AZ의 서버가 요청을 처리하고, 필요에 따라 서버 수를 늘립니다.</p></section><section class=\"concept-notes\" id=\"notes\" role=\"doc-endnotes\"><h2>각주</h2><ol><li id=\"note-1\"><strong>AZ ID</strong> — 계정 간에도 같은 물리적 가용 영역을 가리키는 식별자입니다. 예를 들어 use1-az1과 같은 형식을 사용합니다. <a aria-label=\"각주 1의 본문으로 돌아가기\" class=\"concept-note-back\" href=\"#note-ref-1\">↩</a></li></ol></section><section class=\"references\" id=\"references\"><h2>AWS 공식 문서</h2><ol><li id=\"reference-1\"><a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-infrastructure/latest/regions/az-ids.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">AZ IDs ↗</a></li></ol></section></article><section class=\"related-questions\" id=\"practice\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><div><p class=\"eyebrow\">PRACTICE · ENGLISH</p><h2>연관 문제 5개</h2></div><a href=\"/concepts/quiz/q001/\">문제 전용 화면</a></div><article class=\"question-card\" data-correct=\"0\" data-question=\"Q001\" data-revision=\"1\" id=\"question-Q001\"><div class=\"question-top\"><span class=\"question-no\">Q001</span><span class=\"type-label\">1개 선택</span><a class=\"question-link\" href=\"/concepts/quiz/q001/\">문제 전용 화면</a></div><h3 lang=\"en\">An application must remain available during a prolonged outage of the entire Seoul Region. What is the minimum scope for replication?</h3><fieldset><legend>정답을 선택하세요</legend><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q001\" type=\"radio\" value=\"0\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">A</span><span lang=\"en\">A different AWS Region</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q001\" type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">B</span><span lang=\"en\">A different subnet in the Seoul Region</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q001\" type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">C</span><span lang=\"en\">A different Availability Zone in the Seoul Region</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q001\" type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">D</span><span lang=\"en\">A different ENI in the same Availability Zone</span></label></fieldset><div class=\"question-actions\"><button class=\"check-answer\" type=\"button\">채점하기</button><button class=\"reset-answer\" type=\"button\">선택 지우기</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"feedback\" role=\"status\"></span></div><details class=\"explanation\"><summary>정답과 해설</summary><p><strong>정답 A</strong> · <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a> 분리는 한 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/region/\">리전</a> 안의 장애를 다룬다. <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/region/\">리전</a> 수준 장애는 별도 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/region/\">리전</a> 복제와 전환이 필요하다.</p></details><div class=\"question-tags\"><span>연결 개념</span><a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/region/\">Region</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/dr/\">RPO / RTO</a></div></article><article class=\"question-card\" data-correct=\"3\" data-question=\"Q002\" data-revision=\"1\" id=\"question-Q002\"><div class=\"question-top\"><span class=\"question-no\">Q002</span><span class=\"type-label\">1개 선택</span><a class=\"question-link\" href=\"/concepts/quiz/q002/\">문제 전용 화면</a></div><h3 lang=\"en\">A web tier must withstand a data center failure within one Region. Which deployment is most appropriate?</h3><fieldset><legend>정답을 선택하세요</legend><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q002\" type=\"radio\" value=\"0\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">A</span><span lang=\"en\">Two ENIs on the same EC2 instance</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q002\" type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">B</span><span lang=\"en\">Two instances using one EBS volume</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q002\" type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">C</span><span lang=\"en\">Two instances in a single Availability Zone</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q002\" type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">D</span><span lang=\"en\">Instances deployed across different Availability Zones</span></label></fieldset><div class=\"question-actions\"><button class=\"check-answer\" type=\"button\">채점하기</button><button class=\"reset-answer\" type=\"button\">선택 지우기</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"feedback\" role=\"status\"></span></div><details class=\"explanation\"><summary>정답과 해설</summary><p><strong>정답 D</strong> · <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a>는 독립적인 장애 영역이다. 서로 다른 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a>의 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/subnet/\">서브넷</a>에 웹 인스턴스를 둔다.</p></details><div class=\"question-tags\"><span>연결 개념</span><a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/subnet/\">Subnet / CIDR</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/ec2/\">EC2</a></div></article><article class=\"question-card\" data-correct=\"0\" data-question=\"Q005\" data-revision=\"1\" id=\"question-Q005\"><div class=\"question-top\"><span class=\"question-no\">Q005</span><span class=\"type-label\">1개 선택</span><a class=\"question-link\" href=\"/concepts/quiz/q005/\">문제 전용 화면</a></div><h3 lang=\"en\">A company plans to create one subnet in each of two Availability Zones. Which resource contains the network address range for those subnets?</h3><fieldset><legend>정답을 선택하세요</legend><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q005\" type=\"radio\" value=\"0\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">A</span><span lang=\"en\">A VPC</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q005\" type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">B</span><span lang=\"en\">An EBS volume</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q005\" type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">C</span><span lang=\"en\">A network ACL</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q005\" type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">D</span><span lang=\"en\">An ENI</span></label></fieldset><div class=\"question-actions\"><button class=\"check-answer\" type=\"button\">채점하기</button><button class=\"reset-answer\" type=\"button\">선택 지우기</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"feedback\" role=\"status\"></span></div><details class=\"explanation\"><summary>정답과 해설</summary><p><strong>정답 A</strong> · <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/vpc/\">VPC</a>는 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/region/\">리전</a> 범위이고 그 안의 각 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/subnet/\">서브넷</a>은 한 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a>에 속한다.</p></details><div class=\"question-tags\"><span>연결 개념</span><a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/vpc/\">VPC</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/subnet/\">Subnet / CIDR</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a></div></article><article class=\"question-card\" data-correct=\"2\" data-question=\"Q011\" data-revision=\"1\" id=\"question-Q011\"><div class=\"question-top\"><span class=\"question-no\">Q011</span><span class=\"type-label\">1개 선택</span><a class=\"question-link\" href=\"/concepts/quiz/q011/\">문제 전용 화면</a></div><h3 lang=\"en\">An application runs in two Availability Zones and uses zonal public NAT gateways. If one AZ fails, workloads in the surviving AZ must retain outbound internet access. Which NAT design should the architect use?</h3><fieldset><legend>정답을 선택하세요</legend><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q011\" type=\"radio\" value=\"0\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">A</span><span lang=\"en\">Add only a network ACL</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q011\" type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">B</span><span lang=\"en\">Use a single NAT gateway in AZ A</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q011\" type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">C</span><span lang=\"en\">Deploy a NAT gateway in each AZ and route each subnet to its local NAT gateway</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q011\" type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">D</span><span lang=\"en\">Attach one Elastic IP to both AZs simultaneously</span></label></fieldset><div class=\"question-actions\"><button class=\"check-answer\" type=\"button\">채점하기</button><button class=\"reset-answer\" type=\"button\">선택 지우기</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"feedback\" role=\"status\"></span></div><details class=\"explanation\"><summary>정답과 해설</summary><p><strong>정답 C</strong> · <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a>별 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/nat/\">NAT</a>와 경로는 단일 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a> <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/nat/\">NAT</a> 의존을 제거하고 교차 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a> 트래픽도 줄인다.</p></details><div class=\"question-tags\"><span>연결 개념</span><a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/nat/\">NAT Gateway</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/routes/\">Route Table</a></div></article><article class=\"question-card\" data-correct=\"3\" data-question=\"Q028\" data-revision=\"1\" id=\"question-Q028\"><div class=\"question-top\"><span class=\"question-no\">Q028</span><span class=\"type-label\">1개 선택</span><a class=\"question-link\" href=\"/concepts/quiz/q028/\">문제 전용 화면</a></div><h3 lang=\"en\">Which placement strategy reduces network latency among HPC nodes within one Availability Zone?</h3><fieldset><legend>정답을 선택하세요</legend><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q028\" type=\"radio\" value=\"0\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">A</span><span lang=\"en\">A spread placement group</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q028\" type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">B</span><span lang=\"en\">An EBS snapshot</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q028\" type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">C</span><span lang=\"en\">Instances in different Regions</span></label><label class=\"option\"><input name=\"answer-Q028\" type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/><span class=\"option-letter\">D</span><span lang=\"en\">A cluster placement group</span></label></fieldset><div class=\"question-actions\"><button class=\"check-answer\" type=\"button\">채점하기</button><button class=\"reset-answer\" type=\"button\">선택 지우기</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"feedback\" role=\"status\"></span></div><details class=\"explanation\"><summary>정답과 해설</summary><p><strong>정답 D</strong> · Cluster는 한 <a class=\"term-link\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a> 내 인스턴스를 가깝게 배치한다.</p></details><div class=\"question-tags\"><span>연결 개념</span><a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/placement/\">Placement Group</a> <a class=\"tag\" href=\"/concepts/terms/az/\">AZ</a></div></article></section><nav aria-label=\"용어 이동\" class=\"sequence\"><span><a href=\"/concepts/terms/backup/\">이전 용어 <b>AWS Backup</b></a></span><span><a href=\"/concepts/terms/cost/\">다음 용어 <b>Budgets / Cost Explorer</b></a></span></nav></div></div>"
}
